# Ripped Habbo source art (~4.6MB, 2252 files) — NEVER COMMIT.
# Contains hh_human_item.swf pulled from the live gordon build path, the 2191
# hand-item sprites extracted from it, and archived habbo.com assets (2006
# stylesheets, box-chrome GIFs, navi icons) scraped from the Wayback Machine.
# All of it is Sulake's copyright, kept locally as reference only.
# Fully regenerable: tools/extract-handitems.py re-downloads the SWF and
# re-extracts every sprite; tools/reference/habbo-2006/fetch-assets.sh re-pulls
# the archived web assets.
# NOTE: the 8 baked runtime icons in public/assets/ui/weapons/ stay TRACKED —
# those are shipped product art, not raw rips.
#
# The SCRIPTS that do the re-pulling are tracked too, and so are the plain-text
# records of what they should have pulled. "Fully regenerable" above was false
# while the regenerating script was itself ignored: a fresh clone had no
# fetch-assets.sh and therefore no way to rebuild anything. Our own tooling and
# notes are not Sulake's copyright; the art they download still is.
#
# The rules below are GENERIC across reference sets — they were once hardcoded
# to habbo-2006, so any new directory silently lost its README and scripts the
# moment it was created, which is the same regenerability hole one level up.
# Per set: scripts (*.sh, *.py), notes (*.md) and manifests (*.tsv) at its TOP
# LEVEL are tracked; everything else, including every nested directory of art
# and any scraped .html/.css, stays ignored. *.py is here for the same reason
# as *.sh and was added the moment a survey tool happened to be written in
# Python — the language a script is written in should not decide whether the
# tree stays regenerable.
tools/reference/**
!tools/reference/*/
!tools/reference/*/*.sh
!tools/reference/*/*.py
!tools/reference/*/*.md
!tools/reference/*/*.tsv

# Python bytecode from the tools/ scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc
